<title>POLAND: All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 423 million zlotys against a 900 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold a total of 358 million zlotys worth of T-bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price     --     95.44    91.10     --	83.32</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.46)  (91.12)    --     (83.47)</p>
<p>   new max price     --     95.51    91.14     --	83.65</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.52)  (91.17)    --     (83.50)</p>
<p>   offer		 --     200.0    300.0     --	400.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded     --     133.1     43.8     --	245.8</p>
<p>   bids accepted     --     132.1     43.8     --	181.8</p>
<p>   next auction	--     200.0    300.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
